==Old English==

===Etymology===
Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|wīte|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{m|osx|wīti}}, Dutch {{term|wijte|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{m|goh|wīzi}}, Old Norse {{term|víti|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈwiːte/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=wīte|n|wītu}}

# [[punishment]], [[torment]], [[torture]]
#: ''Hé '''wíte''' wealdeþ. &mdash; He is the disposer of punishment. (He wields punishment.)
# [[plague]], [[disease]], [[evil]], [[injury]], [[pain]]
#: ''Of ðam '''wíte''' gehǽled;'' &mdash; Healed of the disease.
# [[penalty]], [[fine]], [[bote]]: contribution, in money or food, to sustenance of king or his officers
# [[woe]], [[misery]], [[distress]]

